 # Voxel Trilinear Interpolation (SIMD)
 
-Also called: Block Trilinear Sampling, SIMD Trilinear Sampling, Trilinear Interpolation for Brick Sampling, Trilinear Interpolation with AVX, Trilinear Voxel Interpolation
+Also called: Block Trilinear Sampling, BrickDensityRegion Trilinear Interpolation, SIMD Trilinear Sampling, Trilinear Interpolation for Brick Sampling, Trilinear Interpolation for Voxel Sampling, Trilinear Interpolation with AVX, Trilinear Voxel Interpolation
 
 ## Overview
-This method reads a voxel value from a 3D volume using trilinear interpolation with SIMD instructions to accelerate volume rendering [S1, unofficial]. It differs from standard scalar trilinear interpolation by packing four corner values per 128-bit register and computing their contributions in parallel, effectively processing two z-planes simultaneously [S1, unofficial].
+Voxel Trilinear Interpolation (SIMD) retrieves scalar voxel values at arbitrary normalized coordinates within a 3D volume by interpolating between the 8 surrounding corner voxels, optimized for throughput using Single Instruction, Multiple Data (SIMD) instructions [S2, unofficial]. It builds on [Grid Cell Collection via Corner Indices](1518-grid-cell-collection-via-corner-indices.md) by providing the specific arithmetic and memory access patterns required to evaluate the trilinear function efficiently on modern hardware [S2, unofficial]. Unlike standard scalar implementations, this method processes multiple components (e.g., RGB or RGBA) in parallel using vector registers, significantly reducing instruction count for dense volume rendering [S2, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
 **Inputs:**
-- `data`: 1D array of `uchar` (unsigned 8-bit integers) representing the voxel brick [S1, unofficial].
-- `brick_size`: 3D vector `(bx, by, bz)` defining the dimensions of the brick in voxels [S1, unofficial].
-- `blk_pos`: 3D floating-point position within the brick where interpolation is required [S1, unofficial].
-- `bmin`: 3D vector defining the minimum bounds of the volume (for boundary checks) [S1, unofficial].
-- `dims`: 3D vector defining the total dimensions of the volume (for boundary checks) [S1, unofficial].
-- `tf1d`: A 1D transfer function object with a `sampleSimple` method [S1, unofficial].
