 **Data Structures:**
-- The voxel data is stored in row-major order in a 1D `uchar` array of size `(bx+1) × (by+1) × (bz+1)` [S1, unofficial].
-- Index strides for row-major 3D indexing are `stride_x = 1`, `stride_y = bx + 1`, `stride_z = (bx + 1) × (by + 1)` [S1, G, unofficial]. (Note: The source text contains a typo listing `xNext = brick_size.x + 1`; standard row-major indexing requires `stride_x = 1` to correctly fetch adjacent x-voxels [G]).
+- The voxel data is stored in row-major order in a 1D array. The logical brick has dimensions $(bx+1) \times (by+1) \times (bz+1)$ [S2, unofficial].
+- Strides for linear indexing within the brick:
+  - $x_{next} = bx + 1$
+  - $y_{next} = bx + 1$
+  - $z_{next} = (bx + 1) \times (by + 1)$ [S2, unofficial]
+- SIMD registers (128-bit) are used to hold 4 `float` or 16 `uchar` values. The implementation described uses 128-bit registers to process 4 components in parallel [S2, unofficial].
 
